The emission estimate of a match state from the residues `col` that a multiple alignment
places in its column (gaps omitted), with pseudocounts `pc` (Durbin et al., chapter 5;
Laplace's rule is `pc = 1`): `(count a + pc a) / (|col| + ∑ b, pc b)`.

**The binomial family is TP2** (monotone likelihood ratio in the success probability):
for `a ≤ a'` and `0 ≤ p ≤ p' ≤ 1`,
`Binom(a | n, p') Binom(a' | n, p) ≤ Binom(a' | n, p') Binom(a | n, p)`.

The one-sided integrated haplotype homozygosity: the area under the EHH decay curve
in one direction from the focal site. Voight et al.'s iHH integrates in both directions;
see `ihh_twoSided`.

Gierer–Meinhardt activator-inhibitor kinetics in Murray's nondimensional form
`(f, g) = (a - b u + u² / v, u² - v)` on `x = (u, v)` (biologically `a, b > 0` and `u, v > 0`;
at `v = 0` the division gives the junk `u² / 0 = 0`).

**Perfect phylogeny and the four-gamete condition** (Estabrook, Johnson & McMorris 1976;
Gusfield 1991): a binary character matrix on at least two taxa has a perfect phylogeny iff no
two of its columns show all four gametes.

**ABBA–BABA identity** (Patterson et al. 2012; Durand et al. 2011): under independent
sampling of one haplotype per population at derived-allele frequencies `q` (any reals;
frequencies in `[0, 1]` in the biological model), `E[BABA - ABBA] = (q₁ - q₂) (q₃ - q₄)`.

The `N`-normalized score `β̂ j = X_jᵀ y / N` of marker `j`. For a standardized column
(`∑ i, X i j ^ 2 = N`) it is the marginal least-squares estimate of the effect of marker `j`;
in general that estimate has denominator `∑ i, X i j ^ 2` instead of `N`.

Patterson's normalized genotype matrix `(C i j - μⱼ) / √(p̂ⱼ (1 - p̂ⱼ))`. For a
monomorphic marker (`p̂ⱼ ∈ {0, 1}`) the denominator is `0` and the column is the junk value `0`;
Patterson et al. use polymorphic markers only.
